1
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:10,260
=Dungeon Archive=

2
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,640
The killer is...

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,560
Jin Da.

4
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,600
Impressive.

5
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,740
(The killer)

6
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:23,180
(Case resolved: escape successful)

7
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,820
(Jin Da)

8
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:29,740
(Case reconstruction)

9
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:32,200
I'm Jin Da, the killer in this case.

10
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,920
I took a job
at Curator Tui's gallery

11
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:37,560
to find evidence against him

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,600
and expose who he really was.

13
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,280
On 20 May 2026,

14
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,880
while restoring an artifact,

15
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,040
I found something shocking.

16
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:49,160
(Real)
Curator Tui swapped the real artifacts,

17
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,400
(Fake)
then sold them for profit.

18
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,680
I started digging into him

19
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:54,720
and found the stolen money
was only the beginning.

20
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:57,080
(Curator Tui)
He was planning something far worse.

21
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:58,880
On 27 May 2026

22
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,040
at 3PM,

23
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:02,000
I noticed
he'd been going out a lot lately,

24
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,040
barely staying at the gallery.

25
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:03,960
Something felt off.

26
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,510
He was definitely up to something.

27
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,960
As soon as he left,

28
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,440
(Free Appraisals, Restoring History)
I snuck into his office

29
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:11,440
to look for more evidence.

30
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:12,880
I found a hard drive

31
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,240
and took it with me.

32
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:16,000
Once I cracked it, I learned

33
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,480
that he'd use three living treasures
as test subjects.

34
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,280
On 28 May 2026

35
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,280
at 3PM,

36
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:25,760
I was sneaking back into his office

37
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,600
when I overheard a call
with his assistant.

38
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,640
He said, "Jin Da, right"?

39
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,880
"I know how to handle her".

40
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:34,720
He left right after the call.

41
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,880
I snuck back into his office

42
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:40,400
and found a pile of shredded paper
in the trash.

43
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,640
I pieced them together

44
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:44,400
and found a hand-drawn murder plan.

45
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,880
(Gallery Floor Plan)
The gallery had three inner windows,

46
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:49,320
and three outer ones,

47
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:52,760
all perfectly aligned.

48
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,520
Curator Tui sealed the left
and right inner windows

49
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,080
with metal panels,

50
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,160
leaving only the middle one open
as a passage.

51
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,440
Then he built a fake frame

52
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:07,360
beside the real middle window,

53
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,240
covering it with a metal panel too.

54
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:13,200
He placed a display case
in front of the actual center window,

55
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,320
creating an illusion.

56
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:19,640
It made all three windows look sealed,

57
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:22,560
as if the door
were the only way in or out.

58
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,560
Once the door was locked,

59
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:26,120
it became the perfect fake locked room.

60
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,520
(Knockout Spray)
He planned to knock me out,

61
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:32,560
(Gallery)
move me in through the window,

62
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,040
put on the Ghost Armor,

63
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:38,560
enter with a blade,
then lock it behind him.

64
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,760
He'd put the armor on me,

65
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:42,120
kill me,

66
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,160
then escape through the window.

67
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:47,520
(Hallway)
He'd claim the armor had made me

68
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,520
enter the hall and kill myself.

69
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,920
A perfectly staged impossible crime.

70
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,880
(28 May 2026)
At 9PM,

71
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:56,880
Curator Tui messaged me on WeChat.

72
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,760
He told me to meet him
at 10:40AM the next morning

73
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:02,120
(Free Appraisals, Restoring History)
to discuss the auction.

74
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,840
This was it. He was making his move.

75
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,440
Then, I remembered the drawing.

76
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:09,840
He'd planned it all so carefully.

77
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,920
So, why not turn it around

78
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,260
and use his plan against him?

79
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,840
(28 May 2026)
At 11PM,

80
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,000
(Thousand-Faced Eagle King)
in the Eagle King group chat,

81
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,280
(Group Member)
I messaged a random member privately.

82
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:24,360
I said my mission had been approved

83
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,400
and that I needed a partner.

84
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,720
(Invitation accepted)
He was in.

85
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,760
I told him to be there on the 29th,

86
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:32,360
between 10:40AM and 11AM,

87
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:35,440
(Auction Hall, Gallery)
waiting at a set spot in the gallery.

88
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:38,160
His job was to photograph Curator Tui

89
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,080
entering the gallery in armor.

90
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:41,040
Then,

91
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:41,840
leave the photo

92
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,480
(Submit today's check-in photo as usual)
in the hall without raising suspicion.

93
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:47,320
(29 May 2026)
On 29 May at 10:35AM,

94
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,440
I took an Awakening Pill.

95
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,320
For the next hour,

96
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:52,920
no sedative could affect me.

97
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,360
(29 May 2026, 10:40AM)
At 10:40AM,

98
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,520
(Free Appraisals, Restoring History)
I went to Curator Tui's office.

99
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,920
He greeted me warmly

100
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,560
and offered a handshake.

101
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:02,360
(Knockout Spray)
Then, catching me off guard,

102
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,600
he pulled out the knockout spray

103
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,040
and sprayed my face.

104
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:07,040
I faked passing out.

105
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:09,960
(General Waste)
He put me in a trash cart

106
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:12,240
and wheeled me to the gallery.

107
00:04:12,640 --> 00:04:15,480
Then, he lifted me out

108
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,640
and carried me inside
through the window.

109
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:19,830
He climbed back out the same way.

110
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,950
(29 May 2026)
On 29 May at 11AM,

111
00:04:21,950 --> 00:04:23,160
I cracked my eyes open

112
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:26,000
and saw Curator Tui enter
in the Ghost Armor.

113
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,640
He came in through the door

114
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:28,520
and locked it behind him.

115
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,960
As he took off the armor

116
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,480
to put it on me,

117
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:34,720
That was my chance.

118
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:37,480
I grabbed his knife and slit his throat.

119
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:38,880
I got him before he got me.

120
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:41,000
Then, I escaped through the window.

121
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,540
(Jin Jing player log archive)

122
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,100
(Identity: Jin Da)

123
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:44,780
(Tui Exhibition Hall's
Artifact Restorer)

124
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,320
(For the Thousand-Faced Eagle King)

125
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:46,760
I'm player Jin Jing.

126
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:47,800
In this case,

127
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:51,320
I play Jin Da, an artifact restorer
at the Tui Exhibition Hall.

128
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:52,460
- We were inside the gallery.
- Is anyone there?

129
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,560
- We heard someone yelling for help.
- Help!

130
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:55,720
We rushed in and got them out.

131
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:58,720
While we were talking,

132
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:02,000
we heard something strange
inside the gallery.

133
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,120
We followed the trail of blood

134
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,120
and found Curator Tui's body.

135
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:07,960
Everyone froze.

136
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,120
My boss...

137
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:11,480
- Only I knew what had happened.
- How did the boss die?

138
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,600
Because I killed him.

139
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:16,400
When I found out he'd rewritten
the Thousand-Faced Eagle King's story

140
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:19,000
and taken credit

141
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,440
for other heroes' deeds...

142
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,320
Pass them off as his own...

143
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,200
I started investigating him.

144
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,840
(Exposed, forced to fight back)
But he caught on.

145
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,120
His encrypted hard drive was missing.

146
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,200
He designed a locked-room murder

147
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,040
and planned to silence me.

148
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,160
So, I beat him at his own game

149
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,120
and killed him first.

150
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:35,480
Of course, I wasn't about to confess.

151
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:36,860
I acted offended

152
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,700
(Outraged)
and denied any involvement.

153
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:40,480
While everyone examined the body,

154
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:42,960
they found a wound
on Curator Tui's neck.

155
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:45,000
There was blood on the sword,

156
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,080
so they suspected suicide.

157
00:05:46,960 --> 00:05:47,720
Good.

158
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,040
I went along and said,

159
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,180
(Steering the case with others' clues)
"The knife he used".

160
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,960
I made sure
to help everyone gather clues

161
00:05:53,960 --> 00:05:54,880
and analyze the case.

162
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:56,400
At the auction,

163
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,280
everyone found evidence

164
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:59,640
that I'd once caused a scene
at the kite exhibition.

165
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,560
That didn't worry me,

166
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,880
because Ding Tian

167
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:02,760
and Hehe

168
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:04,540
also had grudges against Curator Tui.

169
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:05,760
(Curator Tui's grudges exposed)

170
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:07,680
They'd even threatened him before.

171
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,800
(Using outsiders as a distraction)
As long as I laughed it off,

172
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,600
no one would suspect me.

173
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,280
Then, there was Ning Bo.

174
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,400
It didn't take long

175
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,880
to find clues on him too.

176
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,330
He claimed
he was the ancient Ning Waver,

177
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,480
one of the three treasures.

178
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:23,720
One of the treasures is missing.

179
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:26,120
The second we stepped outside,
Ding Tian's crew grabbed us.

180
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:26,840
Don't move!

181
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,360
In the car,

182
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,880
one of the men holding me
suddenly gave our code phrase.

183
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,070
(Passphrase confirms an ally)
One cause saves all.

184
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,280
I knew right away

185
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:34,400
he was one of us.

186
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:36,800
I had another secret too.

187
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,920
I'm with the modern
Thousand-Faced Eagle Kings group.

188
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,640
We all admired
the Thousand-Faced Eagle King.

189
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:44,080
Turns out, I'd been fooled too.

190
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,840
We had fallen

191
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,040
into the hands
of the criminal R Corporation.

192
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:50,090
We also uncovered

193
00:06:50,090 --> 00:06:51,440
(Connecting the clues)
more crimes linking R Corporation

194
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,280
(R Corporation's ties to Curator Tui)
and Curator Tui.

195
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,640
Conducting biological testing...

196
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:56,320
Once we got back to the crime scene,

197
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:58,120
we started piecing together the timeline

198
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:01,080
and slowly uncovered the secret
of the windows.

199
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,840
I stayed calm and joined right in.

200
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,410
I asked questions
and threw out theories,

201
00:07:06,410 --> 00:07:07,800
(Asking questions
to maintain an innocent front)

202
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,560
That way, they would think

203
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:10,800
I was genuinely trying to find
the killer.

204
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:12,480
Then, I made my move.

205
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,120
(Questioning others to shift suspicion)
I pointed the finger at Hehe

206
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:14,980
and redirected suspicion.

207
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,440
Then, an even better fall guy appeared.

208
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:19,610
(Following suspicions to pick a target)
Ning Waver.

209
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:21,680
No, I should call him Ning Bo,

210
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,080
because he wasn't ancient at all.

211
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:24,880
A modern man.

212
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:26,960
The lie only made him look worse.

213
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,640
Ding was ruled out first,

214
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:32,360
leaving me, Ning Bo, and Hehe.

215
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:34,040
Something Yang Glory said

216
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,680
made Ning Bo look even more suspicious.

217
00:07:35,960 --> 00:07:37,120
Ning panicked.

218
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:39,470
(Amplifying others' suspicions)
I wasn't letting that chance slip away.

219
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,240
While Ning defended himself,

220
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:43,040
I watched everyone else's reactions.

221
00:07:43,880 --> 00:07:46,490
(No longer under suspicion)
At that point, I knew I was safe.

222
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,360
(Voting window)
When it came time to vote,

223
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,560
I voted for Hehe

224
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,160
to add one more wrong vote.

225
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:53,420
(Liu Yuning player log archive)

226
00:07:53,460 --> 00:07:54,180
(Identity: Ning Bo)

227
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:54,940
(Tui Exhibition Hall's Cleaner,
Temporary Guard, Tomb Keeper)

228
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:55,700
(Fulfilling his ancestors' wish)

229
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:56,920
I'm player Liu Yuning.

230
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:00,040
In this case,
I play Ning Bo, a tomb keeper.

231
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,760
I found out someone
had robbed my family tomb.

232
00:08:03,760 --> 00:08:05,120
The remains of my three ancestors,

233
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:08,080
Ning Waver, Ke Stubborn,

234
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,120
and Yang Glory,

235
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,640
had all been stolen

236
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:13,840
by Curator Tui
of the Tui Exhibition Hall.

237
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:16,800
(Cleaning to find his ancestors)
So, I joined the gallery as a cleaner.

238
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:21,120
After rescuing Ning Waver
and taking him home,

239
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,660
I had to get into the auction

240
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:25,400
and save my other two ancestors.

241
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,400
To enter the auction,

242
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,380
I posed as a new guard.

243
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:31,820
(Using a guard's identity
to search the exclusive exhibition)

244
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,520
On my way to the gallery,

245
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:35,150
I spotted blood on the floor.

246
00:08:35,150 --> 00:08:35,880
There's blood here.

247
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:38,370
I followed the trail into the hall

248
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,520
and found Curator Tui's body.

249
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:41,280
Who's that?

250
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:45,080
The footage showed that at 10AM,

251
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:47,120
(Cloud sync every two hours)
Hehe, Ding Tian, and I

252
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:49,120
had all made our patrol rounds.

253
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,240
Other than that,

254
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,440
the only person who entered

255
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,600
(Reconstructing the crime timeline)
was someone in armor at 11AM.

256
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:58,090
Yan had also taken a photo
at 10:55AM

257
00:08:58,110 --> 00:09:00,530
of Curator Tui putting on the armor.

258
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,520
That made it look like

259
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,250
(Tracing Curator Tui's movements)
the victim put on the armor himself,

260
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,640
walked into the hall, and died inside.

261
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,000
By 12:10PM,
when the crime was discovered...

262
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,680
(Cloud sync every two hours)
Because he still hadn't come back out.

263
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,520
That left one big question.

264
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:15,560
How did the killer avoid the cameras

